    vulkan_no_wait_pending_submission_blocks_followup_compute_2026-09-09, 1, "2026-11-13: On release/1.0.0 c8c3e7bc4f1, Linux aarch64 (DGX Spark GB10), Rust seed af717f53d6bce3e5: vulkan_async_submission_contract_spec 3/3; vulkan_async_session_lifecycle_contract_spec 4/5 (red: keeps every async forward visible to the dual-lane ABI audit, a source-text contract). The runtime session ring exists (rt_vulkan_async_session_*), but its only tests use an injected device and vulkan_resident_2d.spl still submits with vulkan_counted_submit_and_wait_fence. Acceptance (live-device ring test: three enqueued before any wait, retire one, fourth without device idle) is unmet and was not written here."
    vulkan_no_wait_pending_submission_blocks_followup_compute_2026-09-09, 2, "2026-11-13 lane uia2: row stays open. Live-device acceptance spec written (test/02_integration/gpu_lane/vulkan_async_ring_live_device_spec.spl, tagged in-development) and run on NVIDIA GB10, release/1.0.0 dc14e46a737: red. Cause 1 fixed: aarch64 Linux seed was linked without --export-dynamic so the dlsym-resolved rt_vulkan_async_session externs failed as not linked; vulkan_async_session_backed_spec 2 examples 2 failures then 2 examples 0 failures, nm -D rt_vulkan 0 then 132. Cause 2 open: on Linux the interpreter runs compute on the gpu.rs dlopen bridge, the ring lives only in the runtime crate whose vulkan feature is macOS-only; supported is 0 by default, and with --features vulkan open still returns 0 because the runtime STATE has no device. Needs one Vulkan owner for both lanes."
    vulkan_no_wait_pending_submission_blocks_followup_compute_2026-09-09, 3, "2026-11-13 lane vk-ring: fixed for the interpreter lane. The dlopen bridge now owns a bounded submission ring (interpreter_extern/gpu_vulkan_async_ring.rs) sharing simple_runtime::vulkan_async_protocol with the compiled runtime ring; rt_vulkan_discard_command is real in the bridge. NVIDIA GB10, release/1.0.0 9100f50e680, same-commit seeds a01a6e3df5426709 (base) and 35aec8193c70d864 (ring): vulkan_async_ring_live_device_spec 1 example 1 failure then 2 examples 0 failures (release-path example added), 10 of 10 serial runs green, in-development tag removed; vulkan_async_session_backed_spec 3 examples 0 failures; vulkan_async_session_lifecycle_contract_spec 5 examples 1 failure on both seeds (runtime_dynload.c source-text example, untouched). 30000 acquire-submit-poll-retire cycles in one process: 0 failures, close 1 (created equals released for fences and command buffers), VmRSS flat over the last 12000 cycles. Not covered: compiled-runtime ring on a live device, unknown-completion on real hardware, bridge telemetry snapshot and abandon_device, vulkan_resident_2d still on the blocking submit."

bug_scope |bug_id, scope, root_layer, note|
    vulkan_no_wait_pending_submission_blocks_followup_compute_2026-09-09, 2, "2026-11-12 lane triage (vulkan-mac lane): required fix is in the Rust runtime owner (VulkanState.quarantined_compute gate, destroy_fence handle-only revocation) = src/compiler_rust + src/runtime, outside this lane's file scope. Pure-Simple side re-confirmed non-authoritative (copied integer handles; cannot release native quarantine). Design docs remain the spec for the runtime owner. No change; open."

